# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend environment
#
# Vite inlines these at BUILD time. They are not read at runtime, so changing
# a value in Vercel does nothing until the next deployment is built.
#
# Anything here ends up in the public JS bundle. Never put a secret in this
# file — the demo passphrase is typed by the user at runtime for exactly that
# reason (see services/apiClient.ts).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Absolute origin of the FastAPI backend, with no trailing slash.
#
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. If it is unset, apiClient falls back to "/api" —
# and this project's vercel.json rewrites /(.*) to /index.html, so that path
# returns the SPA's own HTML with a 200 instead of reaching the API. axios
# then fails to parse it and the UI shows a generic "Network Error", which
# looks identical to the backend being down. A production build with this
# unset logs a loud console error saying so.
#
# Local development:  http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Vercel:             https://<your-backend-host>
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.example.com
